    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe `addContactPreference` method is a textbook fit for this file's established pattern. The `OwnerMapper` already contains a series of `@AfterMapping default void add\u2026(Owner, @MappingTarget OwnerDto)` methods, each deriving one presentation field from the source owner (`addDisplayName`, `addInitials`, `addMembershipNumber`, `addMembershipLevel`, `addLocality`). The new method:\n\n- Uses the identical signature, annotation, naming (`addX`), and Javadoc style as its siblings.\n- Handles exactly one derived field, so it neither duplicates existing logic nor bloats a method into a catch-all.\n- Is placed among the other derivation methods, keeping related logic grouped.\n- Puts the derivation in the right unit \u2014 the DTO mapper is where these presentation-only fields are computed, consistent with the rest of the file.\n\nThe OpenAPI schema addition mirrors the surrounding read-only enum/string property conventions. A maintainer of this codebase would find this natural.",
